<Concept title="Weapon Library (in-game roster)" section="Hierarchies">
  <p>This page is the <strong>curated list of weapons that actually exist in the running game</strong> — the 3D models a player can equip and see. It is intentionally <em>not</em> the full weapon catalog: the 360 <code>WeaponData</code> rows (stats, names, drops) are data, and the complete model/variant browser lives in the <a href="http://192.168.10.36:5173/psz-godot/#/storybook/weapons">web storybook</a>. The roster here is two groups: the <strong>basic PSO weapon-type models</strong> (a handful of base meshes reused across most rows) and the <strong>few <code>ein-</code> weapons</strong> added for testing unique per-weapon models.</p>

  <p>The key words <strong>MUST</strong> / <strong>SHOULD</strong> are used as in RFC 2119. The contract for <em>how</em> weapons are structured (data row vs. archetype) is on the <a href="/hierarchies/weapon">Weapon Hierarchy</a> page; this page is the <em>what</em>.</p>

  <h2>Basic PSO weapon-type models</h2>
  <p>Imported from PSO. ~81 weapon rows share these 14 base meshes (a row varies by stats + <code>tint_color</code>, not model). "Textured" counts surfaces whose material carries an albedo texture; energy weapons (claw, slicer, double saber) are deliberately solid-color/tinted, so 0 is expected for them. <strong>Raw PSO scale</strong> — these need <code>glb_scale ≈ 0.09</code> to match in-game size.</p>
